# Documentation (normative)

Before editing documentation or agent configuration, read:

[`docs/specs/documentation-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/documentation-spec.md)

- Keep exactly the six normative specs under `docs/specs/`; each is self-contained.
- Put engineering guidance in the README nearest its owning code.
- Keep plans, audit/gap reports, historical packs and galleries outside the repository; verify archival copies before removal.
- Keep generated evidence in ignored output directories, with source identity and original provenance.
- `AGENTS.md` indexes specs; each Cursor rule points to one spec. Do not use human guides or archives as requirements.
- Update affected specs with architecture changes. Preserve intended requirements when code drifts; record documentation-only findings externally.
- Backend grant/seed changes require checking portal actor names and graceful forbidden-enrichment handling.
